@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@ A complete, static proofreading and OCR restoration website designed for GitHub
 - **67,000+ spelling-correction mappings** from CSpell's common-misspellings data (US and GB variants), plus **810,000+ domain dictionary words** from 38 bundled CSpell dictionaries (software terms, companies, programming languages, cloud platforms, medical and scientific vocabulary, gaming, licenses and more), shipped gzipped and decompressed in the worker.
 - **Corpus-derived context model for real-word errors**: "their/there/they're"-style confusions are disambiguated by the surrounding words using before/after statistics mined from 3.7 million words of public-domain literature (32 Project Gutenberg classics), combined with grammatical pattern tests for 138 confusion sets.
 - **Frequency-ranked suggestions in 50 languages** (OpenSubtitles top-50k, CC BY-SA — one ranked list per bundled language that has one, up to 50,000 words each): every language's spelling suggestions are ranked by real corpus frequency with the same weighted scorer as English, not just dictionary order.
+- **Inflection-aware spelling across all 86 languages**: a generative morphology layer (`src/core/morphology.js` with per-language tables in `src/core/data/inflections.js`) accepts inflected, declined, and conjugated forms of known words — English plurals and verb forms with doubling/silent-e awareness, German umlaut + declension chains (Häusern → Haus), Cyrillic case and velar alternations (книги → книга), Romance verb reconstructions (hablando → hablar), Turkish agglutination (evlerimdeki → ev), Korean particles (사랑은 → 사랑), Arabic clitics (والكتابات → كتاب), Hindi, Hungarian, Dutch, the Nordic languages, Georgian, Armenian, Hebrew, Greek, and script fallbacks for everything else, including user wordlists. Guard lists keep function-word stems ("thes", "les") out, and typo look-alikes ("runing", "walkeded", "studys", "walkes") stay flagged. When an unknown word does decompose, suggestions offer the main root form (사랑은의 → 사랑).
 - **Ten readability formulas** (Flesch Reading Ease, Flesch-Kincaid, Gunning Fog, SMOG, Coleman-Liau, ARI, Linsear Write, Dale-Chall, FORCAST, Spache) with Dale-Chall and Spache familiar-word lists, displayed in a readability panel.
 - **Sentence-level style analysis**: sentence-length variance, repeated sentence starts, adverb density, nominalization and weasel-word density, and a passive-voice detector — all review-only suggestions.
 - **86 bundled language dictionaries** (14 million+ Hunspell entries): Afrikaans, Aragonese, Arabic, Assamese, Belarusian, Bulgarian, Bangla, Tibetan, Breton, Bosnian, Catalan, Catalan (Valencia), Kurdish (Sorani), Czech, Welsh, Danish, German, Greek, Greek (Polytonic), Esperanto, Spanish, Estonian, Basque, Persian, Faroese, French, Friulian, West Frisian, Irish, Scottish Gaelic, Galician, Gujarati, Guarani, Hebrew, Hindi, Croatian, Hungarian, Armenian, Western Armenian, Interlingua, Indonesian, Interlingue, Icelandic, Interslavic, Italian, Georgian, Kurdish (Kurmanji), Kannada, Korean, Latin, Luxembourgish, Ligurian, Lithuanian, Latgalian, Latvian, Macedonian, Mongolian, Marathi, Norwegian Bokmål, Low German, Nepali, Dutch, Norwegian Nynorsk, Occitan, Odia, Punjabi, Polish, Portuguese, Romanian, Russian, Russian (Petrine orthography), Sanskrit, Sinhala, Slovak, Slovenian, Albanian, Serbian, Serbian (Latin script), Swedish, Swahili, Tamil, Telugu, Turkmen, Turkish, Ukrainian, and Vietnamese — gzipped, loaded on demand for the document's language, with morphology-aware, frequency-ranked suggestions. Most ship as locked `dictionary-*` npm packages; 23 languages without npm packages are vendored from the LibreOffice/dictionaries repository and fetched by the build. American and British English remain fully bundled; Indian English uses the British dictionary and spelling policy.
